    { s: "A volatility smile in which implied volatility is highest at the money and lower on both sides is to be expected when:", c: [ "A single announcement is about to move the price sharply in one direction or the other", "The distribution of the future price has heavy tails on both sides", "Investors are buying puts as protection against a crash", "Volatility is expected to rise over the life of the option" ] },
    { s: "The volatility skew of index options implies that, relative to the lognormal distribution with the at-the-money volatility, the risk-neutral distribution of the index has:", c: [ "A heavier left tail and a lighter right tail", "A heavier right tail and a lighter left tail", "Lighter tails on both sides", "The same tails but a higher mean" ] }
